WEBVTT

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:12.750
Appare, thanks for waiting for me.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:16.330
But Gil's gonna blow up the Valley of Despair!

00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:21.200
Xialian and Al might be in danger!
What now, Appare?!

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:48.040
Reborn?

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:48.580
This machine has two hearts--
a steam engine and a gasoline engine.

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:52.540
"Episode 7: FAKE"
This machine has two hearts--
a steam engine and a gasoline engine.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:53.580
This machine has two hearts--
a steam engine and a gasoline engine.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.500
The one from Al's car!

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:00.790
That's right. The heat from the
gas engine drives the steam engine,

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:03.910
multiplying output over twofold.

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:08.410
I get it! It's not one plus one,
but one times one!

00:02:08.410 --> 00:02:10.370
--That's even less.
--Huh?

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:15.790
Here goes! It's the world's
one and only original hybrid engine!

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:22.330
Holy moly! Where'd you find time to build that?!

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:26.000
The cooling needs work
so we can't use it for long.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.250
Ouch!

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.410
Oh. That gets a little hot.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:30.450
Warn me first!

00:02:30.450 --> 00:02:32.370
--Hototo, water!
--Squeak?

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.540
No, not you! The old one!

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.450
Way to be confusing.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:40.870
Outta the way!

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.160
Now! Do it!

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.450
What a perfect plan.

00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:05.040
Simply the best!

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:15.450
It's a fine morning. Shall we get moving, Gil?

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:29.500
How about a little help here?

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:33.290
I let other people do the menial work.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:35.910
Wake me up when you're done.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:39.790
This junk didn't get here by itself.

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:41.700
Good grief.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.160
Appare?

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.790
Yeah. He shouldn't be this far behind.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.750
He'll come. I know he will.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.620
Yeah.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:59.410
Know any kung fu to bust up this barricade?

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.410
Like that?

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:02.750
Are you mocking me?

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:03.790
Huh?

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.540
There! It's them!

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.080
Yeah! Blast right past 'em!

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:20.330
What's wrong?

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:24.700
If we ride close behind them,
we can slip into the valley.

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:28.120
It's the most logical plan for winning the race.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:33.000
Huh? But what about Xialian and Al?
If we don't let them know--

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:39.040
The engine's not done! If we keep using it,
the car may never run again.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:44.660
That's a problem. We need the
prize money to get back to Japan...

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:47.160
You're okay with that, Appare?

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:52.450
Dammit!

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.080
--You--
--Shut up!

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.410
Appare!

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:15.000
What's the matter?

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.540
Guys, get in your cars! Gil set a trap!

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:21.290
Tsk! Mind your own business.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.620
It's Boss! Give the signal!

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:28.830
Got it!

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:32.910
What the?!

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.910
D-Dylan!

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.910
What have we here?

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.000
Outta the way!

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:51.000
Appare!

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.700
Go ahead! I'll catch up!

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.950
It's toast. We're steam engine only now!

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:02.000
All right! Go, go! Go! Go!
Go! Go! Go! Go! Go! Go!

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.330
Step on it, Appare!

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:21.910
I know!

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:24.660
Hmm?

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:25.870
Huh?

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:30.950
Hey, it's the boss!

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.450
Was there a signal?

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.160
Who cares?! Hurry!

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:37.410
Now! Do it!

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:39.040
Oof!

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:46.910
What are you doing?! Blow it up already!

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:58.160
We'll make it!

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:22.000
Tsk! Whatever... At least
the worst two didn't make it.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.120
Th-That's all I know!

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:26.700
Good grief.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:28.000
Huh?

00:07:30.790 --> 00:07:33.580
Well? Is it an easy fix?

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:36.080
I can fix it.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:37.660
At the supply point.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:38.660
Huh?

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:42.750
Exhaust valve, radiator core, condenser tank...

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:45.950
There's too much broken and too few parts.

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:49.700
I've gotta check if the
driveline was damaged, too.

00:07:49.700 --> 00:07:51.830
You're gonna pull it there?

00:07:51.830 --> 00:07:52.950
That's right.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:56.250
You're kidding! Even if we drove,
it'd take all night just to--

00:07:56.250 --> 00:08:00.410
Shut up! You don't think... I know that?!

00:08:13.000 --> 00:08:14.750
Shit!

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:18.540
I'm gonna make it back to Japan!

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:22.290
Wait for me, Fumi!

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:31.580
I figured this might've happened
since you weren't coming.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:33.910
We'll take turns and tow you.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:37.160
Ooh! What a godsend! Right, Appare?!

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:39.040
No way.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:43.200
What about you guys? If you
keep on driving, you'll be in the lead--

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:45.040
Don't insult me.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:51.160
Dylan and TJ are blocked by rocks
and have to go around Death Valley.

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:53.700
You're not much better off.

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:58.580
Do you think I'd be happy winning
under these circumstances?

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.750
That's right, Appare!

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:06.160
The road is long. We'll have our chance
to catch up with the leaders.

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:12.290
I want to beat you guys fair and square
to prove how good I am.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:15.620
There, it's settled! I'll go grab the rope!

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:20.450
It's not rational to throw away
your lead to help a rival.

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:23.290
I don't care much for easy wins.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:28.580
Doing the impossible is
what makes things interesting.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.620
Hey!

00:09:50.620 --> 00:09:53.080
Quit it! You're making me sick!

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:56.450
Huh? This song changed the whole world!

00:09:56.450 --> 00:10:01.000
If you can't feel the energy,
your soul is dead inside!

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:04.830
No, it's your awful singing that makes me sick.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:08.290
Oh? Let's hear you sing then!

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:11.830
Like it or not, we're in this together!

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.120
Huh?

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:17.500
Wha--?! Hey!

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:20.410
No one drives in front of me!

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:49.620
Once we cross that ridge, we leave Death Valley.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:51.290
We're on a good pace.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:54.160
The path is narrow with lots of cliffs.

00:10:54.160 --> 00:10:57.330
We call it "Bloodstained Pass."

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:59.500
It's too risky at night.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:02.250
We'll camp out and wait for dawn.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:09.870
--Whoa!
--Nice!

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:12.500
You can't fight on an empty stomach.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.200
You're so good at it.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:18.700
Yeah. I lost my mother when I was young.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:22.000
I had to take care of my little sister.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:24.120
I'm sorry.

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.910
It's fine.

00:11:25.910 --> 00:11:28.790
Well, I'll try my hand at hunting.

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:31.370
I'll fetch wood and start a fire.

00:11:31.370 --> 00:11:33.370
I'm going fishing.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:38.870
In times like this,
you're pretty much useless, huh?

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:49.410
I'll help.

00:11:49.410 --> 00:11:53.660
Great. You're definitely smarter than a fish,
so you'll have no problem--

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:57.290
What did you use as bait?

00:11:57.290 --> 00:11:59.040
Potato.

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:00.450
I see.

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:06.330
I thought up a trap that
uses a rope and two trees.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:10.410
Once I set this up on
a few game trails, we'll be--

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:13.160
Nice! Got one!

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:23.660
Appare? Could you take a look at my car?

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:29.950
Thanks for the meal.

00:12:29.950 --> 00:12:32.080
Hey, Appare! Dinner!

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:34.910
Wow! This is tasty, Kosame!

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:40.160
Ah... It's nice to cook for people
who appreciate taste!

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:42.620
How much longer till light?

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:44.370
About six hours?

00:12:44.370 --> 00:12:48.000
Gil and the others will
reach the city around then.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:53.450
If we leave at first light,
we might get there before they leave.

00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:59.160
We'll catch up. I won't allow
some coward to lead the race.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:03.660
I won't let the guys who
killed my father get away.

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:08.410
By the way, I still haven't thanked you.

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:09.290
Huh?

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:13.330
That's right. If you hadn't
told us about the trap,

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:18.160
we would've been in for a detour,
or worse, a funeral.

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:23.120
All I did was tell Appare what I heard.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:24.660
Thanks, Hototo.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:25.830
Squeak?

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:29.700
Oh, sorry! I forgot to feed you, didn't I?

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:37.040
Huh? Hey! That's bad manners, Hototo!

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.250
Hototo?

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.950
The new Hototo.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:42.200
There's so much I could say...

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:45.080
Does original Hototo want some?

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:45.910
Nope.

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:48.410
What, are you jealous?

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:49.950
Hototo's cute.

00:13:49.950 --> 00:13:50.830
--Huh?
--Squeak?

00:13:50.830 --> 00:13:53.660
Cute? Which one?

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:54.910
Both.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:58.040
Yeah? That's only 'cuz he's a child!

00:13:58.040 --> 00:13:59.790
I'm not a child.

00:14:02.660 --> 00:14:04.080
Kosame!

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.330
Mother?

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:36.040
It's surprisingly chilly at night.

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:38.370
Something on your mind?

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:44.410
Back then, why didn't I kill the hybrid engine?

00:14:44.410 --> 00:14:45.370
Huh?

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:49.700
And waiting for Hototo... It wasn't logical.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:53.040
Have I... turned stupid?

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:59.410
What's so funny?! Why did
Al and Xialian even help us out?!

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:04.910
I'm sure they wanna win just as badly.
It just doesn't make sense.

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:07.950
People aren't machines.

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:12.330
We do lots of things that don't make sense.

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:14.290
Do you know why?

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:20.830
Because we're more than a brain.
We think with three different things:

00:15:20.830 --> 00:15:26.080
our heads, our gut, and our heart.

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:29.330
I dunno. That makes my skin crawl.

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:32.200
I'm relieved--

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:35.000
Seeing you like that.

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:36.830
"Eli, Nevada"

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:39.160
"Eli, Nevada"
Where's Mr. Oldin?!

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:43.910
Wh-Who knows? Supposedly,
he left right on schedule.

00:15:43.910 --> 00:15:49.370
Shit! I'm paying him a fortune!
The fearsome Thousand Three, my ass!

00:15:52.910 --> 00:15:55.250
I'm sure he's fine...

00:15:55.250 --> 00:16:00.750
After an eight-hour break,
Gil T. Cigar is preparing to start!

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:04.870
Now then, time for an easy cruise to New York...

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:06.870
No way!

00:16:06.870 --> 00:16:10.200
Dylan and TJ already caught up?!

00:16:10.200 --> 00:16:13.910
Whew! It's just them? Way to scare me!

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:15.290
Al!

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:20.830
It's time for Gil T. Cigar to start!

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:23.830
Huh?

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:27.040
Move! I'll run you over!

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:28.290
Not a chance!

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:30.200
Well, suit yourself.

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:36.120
But if you get hit by this car,
you'll get crushed and mangled to pieces!

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:39.160
Mr. Lyon! What's the problem here?

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:42.120
His goons blew up the Valley of Despair.

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:43.160
What?!

00:16:43.160 --> 00:16:47.250
Hey now! You have any proof they were with me?

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:52.870
Though, even if they were,
is there any rule against blowing stuff up?

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:55.580
There's not a rule for everything, but...

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:56.910
But what?!

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:58.830
No! There's no rule!

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:01.660
In that case, clear the road!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:07.450
Or do you wanna pick a fight with
the Thousand Three in the middle of town?

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:12.910
Let him go. We'll settle this during the race.

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.500
No!

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:21.370
I won't let him go till I find out
who took everything from me!

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:24.000
You gotta death wish, brat?!

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:25.660
Hey, Hototo! This isn't--

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:26.830
Stay away!

00:17:27.790 --> 00:17:32.410
This is... something I have to do!

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:37.450
For the longest time, I journeyed alone--

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:40.200
To take back what was stolen.

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:42.580
Our land, home, horses...

00:17:42.580 --> 00:17:47.370
And once I do, I'm going back
to my mom and family!

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:54.500
But... But, my father's life...!

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:59.870
Those happy times I had with my family...!

00:17:59.870 --> 00:18:02.410
I'll never get that back!

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:14.620
I couldn't care less about your dad.

00:18:14.620 --> 00:18:16.580
What are they doing?

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:18.500
Start racing already!

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:19.620
Outta the way!

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:22.410
--Damn native brat!
--Get lost!

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:33.910
Quit it!

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:36.950
You guys call yourself humans?!

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:52.450
Hey, are you gonna...?

00:18:56.790 --> 00:18:58.620
I won't let you hurt him!

00:19:02.000 --> 00:19:03.580
Stop it!

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:07.870
Please, stop...

00:19:15.200 --> 00:19:19.870
You're sad... I'm sad, too...

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:25.790
I can't... keep up this lie.

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:28.950
I can't lie to the kid...

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.870
Are you all right?

00:19:32.870 --> 00:19:34.290
Yeah...

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:37.500
We were doing so well, too!

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.830
Wh-What's going on here?

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:41.950
He isn't Gil?

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:45.410
He's just someone who borrowed the name?

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:48.950
The secret's out. We're no Thousand Three,

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:53.870
but in America's Midwest,
there's not a soul who hasn't heard of us--

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:57.200
We're the one and only "Bad Brothers."

00:19:57.200 --> 00:19:59.200
Who?

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:01.870
He's my little brother, Tristan.

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:05.410
We're not the ones who killed your father.

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:08.790
We don't know anything about it either.

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:11.950
Sorry about that, brat.

00:20:11.950 --> 00:20:16.040
It's nothing to brag about,
but we don't kill women or children.

00:20:16.040 --> 00:20:19.080
We don't steal from the poor either.

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:22.830
Then why take the name of Gil the Butcher?

00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:26.200
People get scared and steer clear of Gil.

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:29.330
That's pretty ideal for a race, ain't it?

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:32.250
Besides, fancy pants over here...

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:37.290
He loved when we claimed to be Gil,
saying it would liven up the race.

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:40.910
Tsk! You purposely deceived me?!
You're scum that--

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:43.000
We're not scum!

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:49.160
Just outlaws... Like Dylan and TJ
you guys hired to drive.

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:51.290
Got a problem with it?

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:56.910
Mr. Carter, did you not
look into their background?

00:20:56.910 --> 00:21:01.910
Uh, no... Because Gil's
a mysterious man that nobody knows.

00:21:01.910 --> 00:21:06.000
So there you have it. We'll just be on our way.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:08.660
The race goes on.

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:14.000
Hey, does the rule book say you can't
disassemble someone's car?

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:16.580
It doesn't, but...

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:18.450
Okay. Good to know.

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:19.700
Huh?

00:21:26.290 --> 00:21:28.870
That'll take eight hours to fix.

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:31.620
I guess we're even.

00:21:31.620 --> 00:21:34.290
They got us good, Bro.

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:37.250
Didn't I tell you not to call me that?

00:21:37.250 --> 00:21:41.000
Oh yeah! Sorry, Bro!

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:42.040
Sofia...

00:21:42.040 --> 00:21:44.160
I'm glad you're safe.

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:45.790
Could we get some tea?

00:21:45.790 --> 00:21:47.500
Sure!

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:50.700
C'mon, Appare. I'll tow you to the pit.

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:54.330
Thanks. We've got eight hours.
Kosame, come help.

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:55.950
Yeah, yeah.

00:21:58.620 --> 00:22:01.580
No more dangerous stuff.

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:04.080
This revenge...

00:22:04.080 --> 00:22:06.410
It won't bring anyone back.

00:22:06.410 --> 00:22:12.120
Shut up. You don't understand
what it's like for your family to be killed.

00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:16.120
Gil, rather, the Bad Brothers
are left behind in the dust!

00:22:16.120 --> 00:22:20.450
How long can the other cars
maintain their advantage?!

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:47.450
"Next time"

00:23:47.450 --> 00:23:49.910
"Episode 8: HEAVY RAIN"
